# Game development principles

Content and levels are authored by designers and level authors. Code and automation serve the content pipeline; they do not own it. Levels, Blueprints, and assets are the product.

## The one rule

**Default behaviour is create-if-missing, update-in-place. Never delete-and-recreate.**

- **If the resource exists:** reuse it. Update only what config or script drives (volume bounds, transform offset, density, exclusion zones).
- **If it is absent:** create it once, then fall into the "exists" path on every future run.
- **Re-runs must be safe:** multiple runs must not create duplicates, destroy existing instances, or overwrite designer edits.

This is the same contract as the Idempotency Protocol in [00-core-principles.mdc](00-core-principles.mdc), applied to content rather than to scripts.

## Destructive paths are opt-in

Delete-and-recreate is an escape hatch, not a default.

- Gate it behind an explicit config flag or user choice (e.g. `recreate_volume_and_graph: true`). The default must be non-destructive.
- Document what it does and when to reach for it, so the next agent or human does not treat it as the normal path.
- Why: version-controlled assets (`.uasset`, `.umap` in Git LFS) are committed work, and real pipelines are incremental and collaborative. Nuking content breaks iteration and strands anyone with the asset checked out.

Prefer stability and predictability: "run again" should mean *ensure correct state*, not *start over*.

## Respect designer-owned settings

Some settings are the designer's, not the script's.

- **Expose only what iteration needs** (density, bounds, exclusion). Hide or document the rest.
- **No-touch zones:** graph wiring, mesh lists, tag assignment. Document which steps automation cannot perform — see [automation-standards.mdc](automation-standards.mdc) and `docs/PCG/PCG_VARIABLES_NO_ACCESS.md`. Do not overwrite them or assume defaults.
- **Config over code where appropriate:** JSON for values a designer may tune; code applies config rather than hardcoding content decisions. See [docs/CONVENTIONS.md](../../docs/CONVENTIONS.md).

## Where the engine does not expose a setting

Use GUI automation (PyAutoGUI, ref images, Editor-driven scripts) to set it. Do not assume "recreate from scratch" and do not assume "the user will do a one-time setup" — automate it, or log the gap to `docs/Automation/AUTOMATION_GAPS.md` and move on. See [20-full-automation-no-manual-steps.mdc](20-full-automation-no-manual-steps.mdc).

## Checklist

- [ ] Default is create-if-missing, update-in-place; nothing destructive without an explicit opt-in
- [ ] Re-runs create no duplicates and destroy no existing content
- [ ] No step is left "manual for the user" — automated, or logged to `docs/Automation/AUTOMATION_GAPS.md`
- [ ] Config-driven values come from config; anything not automatable is logged with a suggested approach
- [ ] Any destructive option is opt-in, named clearly, and documented

See also: [00-core-principles.mdc](00-core-principles.mdc) (Idempotency), [automation-standards.mdc](automation-standards.mdc) (variables with no access).
